  "description": "231 - Field Maple - Crown lift to a height of 2.5m from ground level.  \r233 - Field Maple - Reduce spread by 0.5m (Not from Tree survey report).\r234 - Field Maple - Crown lift to a height of 2.5m from ground level.\r238 - Cherry - Cut back shrubs to give 1.5m clearance of tree. \r239 - Cherry - Remove basal sucker. \r241 - Sycamore - Crown reduce by 1.5 ? 2m to previous points, Sever and remove a section of Ivy from ground level to a. Height of 1m using hand tools only. \r241a - Holly Group - Cut back all lateral growth back to fence line, approx. 2 - 2.5m\r242 - Ash - Crown reduce by 2 ? 2.5m to previous growth points,  Sever and remove a section of ivy from ground level to a height of 1m, using hand tools only. \r243 - Leyland Cypress group - Sever and remove a section of ivy from ground level to a height of 1m, using hand tools only.\r244 - Ash - Crown reduce by 2 ? 2.5m to suitable growth points,  Sever and remove a section of ivy from ground level to a height of 1m, using hand tools only.\r246 - Ash - Fell to the height of the fence and treat stump using eco plugs. \r248 - Plum - Crown reduce by 1 ? 2m, Crown lift to a height of 2.5m from ground level, Sever and remove a section of Ivy from ground level to a height of 1m using hand tools only. \r249 - Plum - Reduce lateral branches by 1.5m thin ends by 25% to reduce risk of weight related branch failure, Remove deadwood 25mm and greater in diameter.\r(TPO 06, 2016)",
